# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a learning experiment for the latest version of Qiskit noise learning"
msgstr "Construire une expérience d'apprentissage pour la dernière version de Qiskit noise learning"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a learning experiment"
msgstr "Construire une expérience d'apprentissage"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a learning experiment {#build-a-learning-experiment}"
msgstr "Construire une expérience d'apprentissage {#build-a-learning-experiment}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial demonstrates how to build a standard learning experiment from scratch, and use it to learn a model from simulated noisy data.\n"
msgstr "Ce tutoriel montre comment construire une expérience d'apprentissage standard à partir de zéro, et l'utiliser pour apprendre un modèle à partir de données bruitées simulées.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define a gate set on a ring of qubits\n"
msgstr "Définir un ensemble de portes sur un anneau de qubits\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a 2-local Pauli-Lindblad model\n"
msgstr "Choisir un modèle de Pauli-Lindblad 2-local\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the learning experiment\n"
msgstr "Construire l'expérience d'apprentissage\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '4.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate circuits\n"
msgstr "Générer les circuits\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '5.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up local simulation\n"
msgstr "Configurer la simulation locale\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '6.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the program\n"
msgstr "Exécuter le programme\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '7.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze the data\n"
msgstr "Analyser les données\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Running on real hardware\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The circuits below are simulated locally, so this walkthrough needs no IBM Quantum® credentials. To alternatively run it on a real device:\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Exécution sur du matériel réel\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Les circuits ci-dessous sont simulés localement, donc ce pas à pas ne nécessite aucun identifiant IBM Quantum®. Pour l'exécuter plutôt sur un appareil réel :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '  *   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 1**: replace [`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") with a real backend.\n"
msgstr "**Étape 1** : remplace [`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") par un Backend réel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  *   **Step 5**: pass that backend as the executor’s mode, and drop the simulator options.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  *   **Étape 5** : passe ce Backend comme mode de l'executor et supprime les options du simulateur.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"define-a-gate-set-on-a-ring-of-qubits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Define a gate set on a ring of qubits {#1-define-a-gate-set-on-a-ring-of-qubits}"
msgstr "1. Définir un ensemble de portes sur un anneau de qubits {#1-define-a-gate-set-on-a-ring-of-qubits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a [`QiskitGateSet`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-qiskit-gate-set#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGateSet \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGateSet\") from a backend [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) and a subset of its qubits — here a twelve-qubit ring of [`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") — then add one gate to it: a layer of six `CZ` gates covering that ring. By default the gate set is initialized with a preparation gate `P` and a measurement gate `M`.\n"
msgstr "Construis un [`QiskitGateSet`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-qiskit-gate-set#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGateSet \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGateSet\") à partir d'une [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) de Backend et d'un sous-ensemble de ses qubits — ici un anneau de douze qubits de [`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") — puis ajoute-lui une porte : une couche de six portes `CZ` couvrant cet anneau. Par défaut, l'ensemble de portes est initialisé avec une porte de préparation `P` et une porte de mesure `M`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Running on real hardware\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Exécution sur du matériel réel\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Call [`draw()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-gate-set#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.GateSet.draw \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.GateSet.draw\") to see the gate on the device topology: the ring of qubits in the gate set, and which pairs of them the gate entangles.\n"
msgstr "Appelle [`draw()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-gate-set#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.GateSet.draw \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.GateSet.draw\") pour voir la porte sur la topologie de l'appareil : l'anneau de qubits de l'ensemble de portes, et quelles paires d'entre eux la porte intrique.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"choose-a-2-local-pauli-lindblad-model\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Choose a 2-local Pauli-Lindblad model {#2-choose-a-2-local-pauli-lindblad-model}"
msgstr "2. Choisir un modèle de Pauli-Lindblad 2-local {#2-choose-a-2-local-pauli-lindblad-model}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Decide which Pauli-Lindblad generators the noise is allowed to have with a [`PauliLindbladModel`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/models-pauli-lindblad-model#qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel \"qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel\"). Build that generator set from the gate set’s connectivity with [`k_local()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/models-pauli-lindblad-model#qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel.k_local \"qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel.k_local\") — here every 2-local Pauli on connected qubit pairs of the unitary gate, and single-qubit Paulis for preparation and measurement.\n"
msgstr "Décide quels générateurs de Pauli-Lindblad le bruit peut avoir avec un [`PauliLindbladModel`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/models-pauli-lindblad-model#qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel \"qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel\"). Construis cet ensemble de générateurs à partir de la connectivité de l'ensemble de portes avec [`k_local()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/models-pauli-lindblad-model#qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel.k_local \"qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel.k_local\") — ici tous les Paulis 2-locaux sur les paires de qubits connectés de la porte unitaire, et des Paulis à un seul qubit pour la préparation et la mesure.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Display the unknown parameter count for the noise model of each gate.\n"
msgstr "Affiche le nombre de paramètres inconnus du modèle de bruit de chaque porte.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"build-the-learning-experiment\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Build the learning experiment {#3-build-the-learning-experiment}"
msgstr "3. Construire l'expérience d'apprentissage {#3-build-the-learning-experiment}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assemble an [`Experiment`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/experiment-builder-experiment#qiskit_noise_learning.experiment_builder.Experiment \"qiskit_noise_learning.experiment_builder.Experiment\") by composing builder stages. Each stage reads what earlier stages wrote, so order matters:\n"
msgstr "Assemble une [`Experiment`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/experiment-builder-experiment#qiskit_noise_learning.experiment_builder.Experiment \"qiskit_noise_learning.experiment_builder.Experiment\") en composant des étapes de construction. Chaque étape lit ce que les étapes précédentes ont écrit, donc l'ordre compte :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Observe design matrix rank:\n"
msgstr "Observe le rang de la matrice de conception :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"generate-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Generate circuits {#4-generate-circuits}"
msgstr "4. Générer les circuits {#4-generate-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compile the experiment with an [`ExecutorCircuitGenerator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/circuit-generator-executor-circuit-generator#qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator \"qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator\"), generating a [`QuantumProgram`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/quantum-program-quantum-program \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") — one parameterized template circuit per fragment depth.\n"
msgstr "Compile l'expérience avec un [`ExecutorCircuitGenerator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/circuit-generator-executor-circuit-generator#qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator \"qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator\"), ce qui génère un [`QuantumProgram`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/quantum-program-quantum-program \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") — un circuit modèle paramétré par profondeur de fragment.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Draw a template circuit to inspect.\n"
msgstr "Dessine un circuit modèle pour l'inspecter.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/4088c7e98baeb5b56925c6c1f276159582c5f7040fbba76de438b919210bcc5f.png](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-noise-learning/4088c7e98baeb5b56925c6c1f276159582c5f7040fbba76de438b919210bcc5f.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/4088c7e98baeb5b56925c6c1f276159582c5f7040fbba76de438b919210bcc5f.png](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-noise-learning/4088c7e98baeb5b56925c6c1f276159582c5f7040fbba76de438b919210bcc5f.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"set-up-local-simulation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Set up local simulation {#5-set-up-local-simulation}"
msgstr "5. Configurer la simulation locale {#5-set-up-local-simulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To define the noise model for simulation, we use the generators already in the model with random rates to construct a [`PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap).\n"
msgstr "Pour définir le modèle de bruit de la simulation, nous utilisons les générateurs déjà présents dans le modèle avec des taux aléatoires pour construire une [`PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Those maps are as wide as the device, since the model is expressed in `backend`’s qubit indexing, but the simulator wants each map to be as wide as the gate it applies to, with Pauli indices running over the gate’s qubits in ascending physical order. Narrow them with [`keep_qubits()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap#keep_qubits), which traces out everything off the ring:\n"
msgstr "Ces maps ont la largeur de l'appareil, puisque le modèle est exprimé dans l'indexation des qubits de `backend`, mais le simulateur veut que chaque map ait la largeur de la porte à laquelle elle s'applique, avec des indices de Pauli parcourant les qubits de la porte dans l'ordre physique croissant. Réduis-les avec [`keep_qubits()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap#keep_qubits), qui trace tout ce qui est hors de l'anneau :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simulator names a layer’s noise by the box instruction the layer was built from, which [`to_instruction()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-qiskit-gate#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGate.to_instruction \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGate.to_instruction\") returns for any gate in the gate set. Pair each box with its map, use the stabilizer simulation method, and set `seed_simulator` to make the simulated data reproducible:\n"
msgstr "Le simulateur nomme le bruit d'une couche d'après l'instruction de boîte à partir de laquelle la couche a été construite, que [`to_instruction()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-qiskit-gate#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGate.to_instruction \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGate.to_instruction\") renvoie pour toute porte de l'ensemble de portes. Associe chaque boîte à sa map, utilise la méthode de simulation stabilizer et définis `seed_simulator` pour rendre les données simulées reproductibles :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"run-the-program\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Run the program {#6-run-the-program}"
msgstr "6. Exécuter le programme {#6-run-the-program}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the program, then format the results with [`collect()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/circuit-generator-executor-circuit-generator#qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator.collect \"qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator.collect\"), to produce a [`Fit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/analysis-fit#qiskit_noise_learning.analysis.Fit \"qiskit_noise_learning.analysis.Fit\") — the container the analysis stages read from and write to.\n"
msgstr "Exécute le programme, puis formate les résultats avec [`collect()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/circuit-generator-executor-circuit-generator#qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator.collect \"qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator.collect\"), pour produire un [`Fit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/analysis-fit#qiskit_noise_learning.analysis.Fit \"qiskit_noise_learning.analysis.Fit\") — le conteneur dans lequel les étapes d'analyse lisent et écrivent.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This step is the same whether the executor is pointed at a simulator or at a real device.\n"
msgstr "Cette étape est la même que l'executor pointe vers un simulateur ou vers un appareil réel.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"analyze-the-data\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. Analyze the data {#7-analyze-the-data}"
msgstr "7. Analyser les données {#7-analyze-the-data}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build an analysis pipeline around nonnegative least squares fitting of the model.\n"
msgstr "Construis un pipeline d'analyse autour de l'ajustement du modèle par moindres carrés non négatifs.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plot the measured observable means against their fitted exponentials, one subplot per `CZ` pair, to see whether the decays being fitted are exponential at all.\n"
msgstr "Trace les moyennes d'observables mesurées face à leurs exponentielles ajustées, un sous-graphique par paire `CZ`, pour voir si les décroissances ajustées sont bien exponentielles.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Swap `exponential_fit` for `model_prediction` to compare the same data against the decays implied by the rates that came out of the non-negative least squares solve.\n"
msgstr "Remplace `exponential_fit` par `model_prediction` pour comparer les mêmes données aux décroissances impliquées par les taux issus de la résolution par moindres carrés non négatifs.\n"
